      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "When writing integration tests that rely on a loaded Spring "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", it is often sufficient to test against a single context. However, there are times when it is beneficial or even necessary to test against a hierarchy of "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " instances. For example, if you are developing a Spring MVC web application, you typically have a root "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " loaded by Spring’s "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ContextLoaderListener"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " and a child "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WebApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " loaded by Spring’s "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "DispatcherServlet"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". This results in a parent-child context hierarchy where shared components and infrastructure configuration are declared in the root context and consumed in the child context by web-specific components. Another use case can be found in Spring Batch applications, where you often have a parent context that provides configuration for shared batch infrastructure and a child context for the configuration of a specific batch job."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "You can write integration tests that use context hierarchies by declaring context configuration with the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@ContextHierarchy"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " annotation, either on an individual test class or within a test class hierarchy. If a context hierarchy is declared on multiple classes within a test class hierarchy, you can also merge or override the context configuration for a specific, named level in the context hierarchy. When merging configuration for a given level in the hierarchy, the configuration resource type (that is, XML configuration files or component classes) must be consistent. Otherwise, it is perfectly acceptable to have different levels in a context hierarchy configured using different resource types."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "The remaining JUnit Jupiter based examples in this section show common configuration scenarios for integration tests that require the use of context hierarchies."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Single test class with context hierarchy"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "strong",
            "roles": []
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ControllerIntegrationTests"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " represents a typical integration testing scenario for a Spring MVC web application by declaring a context hierarchy that consists of two levels, one for the root "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "WebApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (loaded by using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "TestAppConfig"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Configuration"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " class) and one for the dispatcher servlet "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "WebApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (loaded by using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "WebConfig"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Configuration"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " class). The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "WebApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " that is autowired into the test instance is the one for the child context (that is, the lowest context in the hierarchy). The following listing shows this configuration scenario:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension.class)\n@WebAppConfiguration\n@ContextHierarchy({\n\t@ContextConfiguration(classes = TestAppConfig.class),\n\t@ContextConfiguration(classes = WebConfig.class)\n})\nclass ControllerIntegrationTests {\n\n\t@Autowired\n\tWebApplicationContext wac;\n\n\t// ...\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension::class)\n@WebAppConfiguration\n@ContextHierarchy(\n\tContextConfiguration(classes = [TestAppConfig::class]),\n\tContextConfiguration(classes = [WebConfig::class]))\nclass ControllerIntegrationTests {\n\n\t@Autowired\n\tlateinit var wac: WebApplicationContext\n\n\t// ...\n}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "open",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Class hierarchy with implicit parent context"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "strong",
            "roles": []
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The test classes in this example define a context hierarchy within a test class hierarchy. "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "AbstractWebTests"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " declares the configuration for a root "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "WebApplicationContext"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in a Spring-powered web application. Note, however, that "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "AbstractWebTests"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " does not declare "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@ContextHierarchy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". Consequently, subclasses of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "AbstractWebTests"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " can optionally participate in a context hierarchy or follow the standard semantics for "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@ContextConfiguration"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "SoapWebServiceTests"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "RestWebServiceTests"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " both extend "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "AbstractWebTests"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and define a context hierarchy by using "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@ContextHierarchy"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". The result is that three application contexts are loaded (one for each declaration of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@ContextConfiguration"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "), and the application context loaded based on the configuration in "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "AbstractWebTests"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is set as the parent context for each of the contexts loaded for the concrete subclasses. The following listing shows this configuration scenario:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension.class)\n@WebAppConfiguration\n@ContextConfiguration(\"file:src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/applicationContext.xml\")\npublic abstract class AbstractWebTests {}\n\n@ContextHierarchy(@ContextConfiguration(\"/spring/soap-ws-config.xml\"))\npublic class SoapWebServiceTests extends AbstractWebTests {}\n\n@ContextHierarchy(@ContextConfiguration(\"/spring/rest-ws-config.xml\"))\npublic class RestWebServiceTests extends AbstractWebTests {}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension::class)\n@WebAppConfiguration\n@ContextConfiguration(\"file:src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/applicationContext.xml\")\nabstract class AbstractWebTests\n\n@ContextHierarchy(ContextConfiguration(\"/spring/soap-ws-config.xml\"))\nclass SoapWebServiceTests : AbstractWebTests()\n\n@ContextHierarchy(ContextConfiguration(\"/spring/rest-ws-config.xml\"))\nclass RestWebServiceTests : AbstractWebTests()"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Kotlin"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "open",
        "id": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Class hierarchy with merged context hierarchy configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "strong",
            "roles": []
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The classes in this example show the use of named hierarchy levels in order to merge the configuration for specific levels in a context hierarchy. "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BaseTests"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " defines two levels in the hierarchy, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "parent"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "child"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ExtendedTests"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " extends "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "BaseTests"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and instructs the Spring TestContext Framework to merge the context configuration for the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "child"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " hierarchy level, by ensuring that the names declared in the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "name"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute in "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@ContextConfiguration"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " are both "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "child"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". The result is that three application contexts are loaded: one for "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/app-config.xml"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", one for "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/user-config.xml"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", and one for "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "{\"/user-config.xml\", \"/order-config.xml\"}"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". As with the previous example, the application context loaded from "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/app-config.xml"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is set as the parent context for the contexts loaded from "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/user-config.xml"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "{\"/user-config.xml\", \"/order-config.xml\"}"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". The following listing shows this configuration scenario:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension.class)\n@ContextHierarchy({\n\t@ContextConfiguration(name = \"parent\", locations = \"/app-config.xml\"),\n\t@ContextConfiguration(name = \"child\", locations = \"/user-config.xml\")\n})\nclass BaseTests {}\n\n@ContextHierarchy(\n\t@ContextConfiguration(name = \"child\", locations = \"/order-config.xml\")\n)\nclass ExtendedTests extends BaseTests {}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "java",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
                      [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "Java"
                        }
                      ]
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "context": "listing",
                          "id": null,
                          "inlines": [
                            {
                              "kind": "text",
                              "value": "@ExtendWith(SpringExtension::class)\n@ContextHierarchy(\n\tContextConfiguration(name = \"parent\", locations = [\"/app-config.xml\"]),\n\tContextConfiguration(name = \"child\", locations = [\"/user-config.xml\"]))\nopen class BaseTests {}\n\n@ContextHierarchy(\n\tContextConfiguration(name = \"child\", locations = [\"/order-config.xml\"])\n)\nclass ExtendedTests : BaseTests() {}"
                            }
                          ],
                          "language": "kotlin",
                          "roles": [],
                          "title": null
                        }
                      ],
                      "checkbox": null,
                      "inlines": []
                    },
                    "terms": [
